    "searchCoverage": "Official Cloudflare DNS API at https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4 with Authorization Bearer. Native healthcheck is GET /zones, a cheap defined-action read that also matches the pinned validator fallback when GET /user/tokens/verify is unavailable for account-owned tokens. HTTP 200 envelopes with a populated errors array are demoted via bodyErrorPaths. DNS record create/update/delete are omitted as writes. Dated 2026-09-13 incident search recorded Cloudbleed (2017) and Salesloft/Drift (2025-08/09).",
    "incidents": [
      {
        "date": "2025-09-02",
        "source": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/response-to-salesloft-drift-incident/",
        "finding": "Salesloft Drift OAuth access to Cloudflare's Salesforce support tenant between 2025-08-12 and 2025-08-17. 104 API tokens found in support-case text were rotated; Cloudflare reported no suspicious activity on those tokens.",
        "limitation": "Historical third-party CRM exposure; not a documented compromise of api.cloudflare.com itself. This is not a breach-free claim."
      },
      {
        "date": "2017-02-23",
        "source": "https://blog.cloudflare.com/incident-report-on-memory-leak-caused-by-cloudflare-parser-bug/",
        "finding": "Cloudbleed parser bug leaked HTTPS memory. Patched in 2017.",
        "limitation": "Historical; not a current unresolved compromise."
      }
    ],
